<h2>How to get started, step by step</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Choose your license.</strong> School, for an institution with a single campus, or Volume, for multiple campuses or school networks.</li>
<li><strong>Activate the platform.</strong> The customer portal shows your license code, expiration date and number of seats.</li>
<li><strong>Register your team.</strong> Add teachers and school leaders from the portal, including by bulk upload.</li>
<li><strong>Start with a pilot grade.</strong> Choose one grade and two or three subjects to go through the full cycle for one term: textbook, planning, lesson, assessment and report card.</li>
<li><strong>Evaluate and expand.</strong> At the end of the term, review with the teachers what worked and extend its use to the other grades.</li>
</ol>
<p>If your school still consolidates grades or tracking in spreadsheets during the transition, my <a href="/excel/">Excel for teachers</a> resources may come in handy.</p>

<h2>Good practices and precautions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>The teacher has the final say.</strong> Assisted marking and feedback are suggestions: review and approve them before they reach your students.</li>
<li><strong>Put what the AI generates in context.</strong> A well-written lesson plan doesn’t replace your knowledge of the group; adapt examples, timings and materials.</li>
<li><strong>Protect students’ data.</strong> EduNova handles data in accordance with Law 1581 of 2012 (Colombia’s data protection law) and the school owns its information; even so, decide who has access to what and avoid sharing sensitive information outside the platform.</li>
<li><strong>Mind your language with families.</strong> Review report cards and newsletters before sending them: they should be clear, respectful and useful.</li>
<li><strong>Support adoption.</strong> Make the most of the initial training and set aside time for teachers to share what works for them.</li>
</ul>
<p>To dig deeper into the responsible use of artificial intelligence at school, visit the <a href="/ia-para-docentes/">AI and technology for teachers</a> hub.</p>

<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
<h3>Do I need to install anything to use EduNova?</h3>
<p>No. EduNova runs in the browser on computers, tablets and phones; all you need is an internet connection.</p>
<h3>What is EduNova Studio?</h3>
<p>It’s the module for creating your own digital textbooks, reflecting the school’s teaching model, identity and context; it’s included in the Volume License.</p>
<h3>Does it include preparation for the national standardized exams?</h3>
<p>Yes. The Assessments module lets you create practice tests structured like the national exam, with question banks by competency and different difficulty levels.</p>
<h3>How is students’ data handled?</h3>
<p>In accordance with Law 1581 of 2012: the school owns its information and can request its export or deletion.</p>
<h3>How is it different from AulaMágica IA?</h3>
<p>EduNova integrates the full learning cycle in eight connected modules, while AulaMágica IA is a set of AI tools for teachers’ day-to-day work.</p>

<h2>Conclusion</h2>
<p>EduNova offers something many schools need: to stop working in silos. When planning, lessons, assessment, remedial work and communication with families are connected, teachers get time back and the school gains a real view of learning. Explore the modules and licenses on the <a href="https://www.grupologiclatam.com/productos/edunova/?utm_source=edwinortiz.net&amp;utm_medium=articulo&amp;utm_campaign=edunova-ia-planear-ensenar-evaluar-colegio" rel="noopener">official EduNova page</a>. And if you’d like your students to create their own materials too, check out <a href="/bookstudio-libros-interactivos-aula/">BookStudio</a>.</p>
